# tally 2.1.8 §14, P54 (the final check, T's rc_refusal_words_differ g1): a window's hole asks the read's own
# question: a fixed-day leg that oa's window reaches makes flows of ob and of pot holes asking for flows of ob and
# flows of pot (a balance asks for a balance: L4_4_refusal_words_differ g3). 4d9223e8 asked both for a balance.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind savings: place PLN min 0
place pot: savings lives 2025-01-01..
place jar: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wa: date
input db: date
input amt: money PLN
input small: money PLN
input amt2: money PLN

move oa: transfers
  on wa
  leg cash from pot to jar amount small

move ob: transfers
  on db
  leg cash from pot to world amount amt2

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  small = 10.00 PLN "s"
  amt2 = 200.00 PLN "s"
  wa = window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) "s"
  db = 2026-04-07 "s"
  opening[pot] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[jar] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask g1: flows(ob, 2026-04)
ask fp: flows(pot, 2026-04)
=== expect
fp: ?"date within window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) not precise enough for flows of pot" (oa)
  cut 2026-01-01
g1: ?"date within window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) not precise enough for flows of ob" (oa)
  cut 2026-01-01
warning: WARN-UNREAD input amt is read by nothing
